WEBVTT

00:13:58.121 --> 00:14:01.121
that go to make up a leopard, for example.

00:14:01.121 --> 00:14:04.037
So what could that lead to?

00:14:04.079 --> 00:14:06.829
Give me an example
of when that AI is working,

00:14:06.829 --> 00:14:08.871
what do you picture happening in the world

00:14:08.912 --> 00:14:11.121
in the next five or 10 years
that excites you?

00:14:11.537 --> 00:14:14.037
Jeff Dean: I think
the grand challenge in AI

00:14:14.079 --> 00:14:16.454
is how do you generalize
from a set of tasks

00:14:16.496 --> 00:14:17.912
you already know how to do

00:14:17.954 --> 00:14:19.162
to new tasks,

00:14:19.204 --> 00:14:21.746
as easily and effortlessly as possible.

00:14:21.746 --> 00:14:24.996
And the current approach of training
separate models for everything

00:14:24.996 --> 00:14:28.162
means you need lots of data
about that particular problem,

00:14:28.162 --> 00:14:30.704
because you're effectively trying
to learn everything